Ladybird measures an auto-width block button’s contents
before it treats the button’s width as definite. Blink’s
ShouldBlockContainerChildStretchAutoInlineSize excludes
native buttons from ordinary block stretching. WebKit’s
RenderBox::sizesLogicalWidthToFitContent includes auto-width
buttons. Gecko’s nsIFrame::IsReplaced recognizes button elements, and
ReflowInput requests shrink-wrapping for an in-flow replaced box outside
flex and grid containers.

Chrome 158.0.8127.37, Firefox 151.0, and WebKit 26.5 sized the flex
button in the meow.camera reduction to 29.31px, 29.33px, and 24.19px
respectively. Removing its aspect ratio left each width unchanged. None
stretched the button to the 400px containing block.
